   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "cice_dynamics_bgrid_pins",
     "description": "Instantaneous B-grid pin of the traced step-2 dynamics state at t = 0 (time_span {0,0}): the strain rates, the stress integrals, the Hibler strength and the ocean-ice stress are pinned against the instrumented dump. Initial conditions: the momentum states uvel/vvel = the momentum dump's uold/vold (the U(4,4) = (0,0) convention: the dump cell (4,4) carries zero velocity, matching the transport dump's U(4,4) = (0,0) -- local cell (3,1) is zero; the stress-dump uvel column equals momentum uold at U(i,j) exactly at every overlapping point) and the EVP stress states stressp/stressm/stress12 = the stress dump's newp/newm/new12 ksub1 corner fields. Parameter overrides: the full-domain aicen/vicen/vsnon (the transport dump's t_entr state), the free-name B-grid geometry (dxT/dyT/cxp/cyp/cxm/cym/dxhy/dyhx from the stress-dump corner-1 columns, HTE/HTN = (3*cyp-cym)/4, (3*cxp-cxm)/4 from the transport pins, uarear from the momentum dump) and the momentum-dump aiX/uocn/vocn; the overrides cover all 15 cells so that m = 917*vice + 330*vsno > 0 and DminTarea = deltaminEVP*dxT*dyT > 0 everywhere (the default zeros would leave 0/0 NaNs in the momentum and viscosity chains). Pins: divu/tension/shear at local cell (2,2) = global (3,5), corners 1-4 (12 values; the strain_rates corner combinations of ice_dyn_shared.F90:2148-2175, area-weighted m^2/s), strintx/strinty at local (1,1) = the U point U(2,4) (the stepu stress integrals, ice_dyn_evp.F90:1698-1765), the Hibler strength P at T cell (2,4) (local (1,1)) = 546804.85434316727 from aice = 0.99429235690336681, vice = 22.288232303770492 (the traced run's actual Rothrock strength dumps 321248.866048; the Hibler-form pin is the formulation pin, see README.md), and vrel/taux/tauy/Cb at U(2,4) with the dump's aiX = 0.88645316794602425, uocn = 1.5095414346433244e-05, vocn = -0.00097471507663916184 (the full dyn_finish taux/tauy form, F90:1345-1348; the dump's stepu partials vrel*waterx/y are pinned in the cap test cice_coupling.esm). Tolerance rel 1e-12 throughout (the rules reproduce the Fortran algebra exactly on the traced subdomain).",
